# Line endings are LF in the repository and LF in the working tree, on every
# machine. Without this, git on Windows checks files out with CRLF, and Pint
# then reports every PHP file as needing a line-ending fix while CI on Linux
# sees nothing wrong — a check that passes or fails depending on who runs it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, and not to be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.mp3 binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.gz binary
